WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:06.100
Let's review how we
transfer stitches manually.

2
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.900
Using the double-eye needle,
we position it opposite the ribber

3
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:15.100
and insert the hook of the needle
in the hole of the tool.

4
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:20.260
Pull up the needle and put
the stitch behind the latch.

5
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:25.540
Push down on the needle to slip
the stitch onto the tool.

6
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:29.180
Then slip the stitch
to the other end of the tool.

7
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.060
Position the eye of the tool over the hook

8
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:37.360
of the target needle
and slip the stitch off.

9
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:44.100
Now we can do the same thing
by using two transfer tools.

10
00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:49.260
Position the eyes of the first tool
over the needles to be transferred.

11
00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.940
Pull up to get the stitches
behind the latches.

12
00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.660
Push down to transfer
the stitches to the tool.

13
00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.420
Insert the prongs of a second tool

14
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:08.340
in the stitches and transfer
the stitches to the second tool.

15
00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.100
Set the first tool aside.

16
00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.800
Slip the eyes of the tool over the hooks

17
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.240
to the target needles and slip
the stitches onto the needles.

